    "q1_propagation_observed": "Yes in condition C: 556 of 1296 spikes were non-stimulated and 82 motor neurons fired. Not universal; B, D, E and baselines did not recruit the decoder pools.",
    "q2_motor_populations_activated": "Yes in C: 71 LEFT/RIGHT/JUMP motor neurons (27/32/12) plus 11 unassigned motor neurons.",
    "q3_left_right_jump_differ": "Yes: whole-span active fractions 14.6% / 17.2% / 60.0%; per-window LEFT and RIGHT stay below 0.20 while JUMP exceeds it.",
    "q4_decoder_distinguishes": "Yes in this sample: JUMP in 4 of 5 windows, NEUTRAL after the stimulus; every matched control is NEUTRAL. Not universal.",
    "q5_non_motor_activity": "Yes: 82 of 164 active neurons are non-motor (64 stimulated plus 18 other), with 64 non-stimulated non-motor spikes.",
    "q6_baseline_motor_activity": "No: conditions A and F produced zero spikes with and without 50 pA background and noise.",
    "q7_seed_stability": "Conditions A-E are deterministic; the noise-only control F was silent under three seeds, so variability is zero because no spontaneous activity exists.",
    "q8_threshold_sensitivity": "Decoded action stable across thresholds 1, 5 and 10; spike and motor counts change by up to about 20%.",
    "q9_sign_sensitivity": "Yes, completely: flipping the 64 stimulated neurons to inhibitory leaves 605 directly driven spikes and zero downstream or motor spikes; all NEUTRAL.",
    "q10_weight_sensitivity": "Yes, strongly: action survives primary and uncapped power transforms but disappears under linear, log1p and power-0.5 transforms.",
    "q11_matched_random": "Yes in this sample: C produces 492 motor spikes, D produces 0, E produces 0. Single seeded draws, not distributions.",
    "q12_shuffled_controls": "Yes in this sample: E, the shuffled descending assignment, is NEUTRAL; the signal is tied to the connectivity-ranked VNC intrinsic candidate."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Verified-only coverage: 44.5% of threshold-5 edges and 45.4% of synapses are signed; 62.1% of neurons are unannotated. The result describes a signed subnetwork, not the whole connectome.",
    "Sign dependence: the entire positive result disappears when the stimulated neurons are treated as inhibitory. Sign is a declared prior, not a measured postsynaptic effect.",
    "Transform dependence: the decoded action disappears under several plausible monotone weight transforms. Weights are declared calibrations, not conductances.",
    "Candidate selection: groups are 64 structurally ranked neurons, not identified command neurons; the descending top-64 is heavily unannotated.",
    "One positive condition: only the VNC intrinsic group recruited the decoder pools; robustness to group size and selection rule is untested.",
    "Single control draws: D and E are one seeded draw each, so zero motor spikes is a matched negative control, not a distribution.",
    "Pool imbalance: JUMP has 20 neurons versus 185 and 186 for LEFT and RIGHT; active-fraction scoring favours small pools though thresholds were fixed in advance.",
